{"schema_version":1,"seq":5,"event_id":"evt_20260524_211946_0005","run_id":"2026-05-24-fix-generated-lines-base-ref-head","at":"2026-05-24T21:19:46-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"ArtifactWritten","status":"planning","payload":{"artifact_key":"plan","path":"/Users/timothy.shee/GitHub/new-tech-monorepo/agentic-development-task-system-v3__ai/agent-workbench-live/runs/2026-05-24-fix-generated-lines-base-ref-head/plan.md","summary":"template staged"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":6,"event_id":"evt_20260524_212304_0006","run_id":"2026-05-24-fix-generated-lines-base-ref-head","at":"2026-05-24T21:23:04-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-001","text":"`git rev-parse --verify HEAD` against the source repo at `/start` returns the same 40-char SHA that `git worktree add ... HEAD` will fork from.","reason":"Git semantics \u2014 `worktree add <path> HEAD` resolves HEAD to its current commit and creates the new branch off that. No concurrent commit can land between the rev-parse and the worktree-add in normal local usage.","impact":"medium. If wrong, the captured SHA could be off by one commit. We accept this as an inherent local-tool race.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":7,"event_id":"evt_20260524_212304_0007","run_id":"2026-05-24-fix-generated-lines-base-ref-head","at":"2026-05-24T21:23:04-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-002","text":"Existing `metadata.yaml` files under `runs/*/` will continue to load via `metadata.load()` without modification when we add an optional `base_ref_sha` field to the schema.","reason":"`metadata.py:_validate` only enforces the `REQUIRED_TOP_LEVEL` keys + status enum. Nested `target.repo.*` is not strictly validated by the loader; the YAML schema in `schemas/run-metadata.yaml` is descriptive only at the moment.","impact":"low. Verified by inspection of `metadata.py:68-77`.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":8,"event_id":"evt_20260524_212304_0008","run_id":"2026-05-24-fix-generated-lines-base-ref-head","at":"2026-05-24T21:23:04-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-003","text":"Existing E2E snapshot tests do not pin the literal contents of `metadata.yaml` such that adding a new optional field breaks them.","reason":"Best assumption \u2014 snapshot tests typically compare run-output structure not the full metadata blob. To verify during build by running `test_e2e.py` early.","impact":"medium. If wrong, snapshot regen is cheap.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":9,"event_id":"evt_20260524_212304_0009","run_id":"2026-05-24-fix-generated-lines-base-ref-head","at":"2026-05-24T21:23:04-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-004","text":"The dogfood run's worktree at `~/GitHub/LOCAL_worktrees/new-tech-monorepo/agent-workbench-live/worktrees/...` may or may not still exist on disk; QA-3 is best-effort regardless.","reason":"The brief explicitly says best-effort. Worktree pruning is a normal user action.","impact":"low.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":10,"event_id":"evt_20260524_212304_0010","run_id":"2026-05-24-fix-generated-lines-base-ref-head","at":"2026-05-24T21:23:04-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-005","text":"There is no `agent-workbench doctor` command that hard-validates every field in the YAML schema against `schemas/run-metadata.yaml`. (To verify in QA-4.)","reason":"Spot-check of `lib/cli/cmd_doctor.py` would confirm; the validate path in `metadata.py:_validate` is shallow.","impact":"low.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":11,"event_id":"evt_20260524_212304_0011","run_id":"2026-05-24-fix-generated-lines-base-ref-head","at":"2026-05-24T21:23:04-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-001","decision":"Add `target.repo.base_ref_sha` (Option (a) from the brief) rather than rewriting `target.repo.base_ref` in place.","rationale":"Brief explicitly prefers (a). Additive schema; keeps the symbolic-ref intent legible for humans reading `metadata.yaml`; doesn't lose information.","alternatives_considered":"(b) rewrite `base_ref` in place at `/start`; (c) compute SHA at metrics time only.","why_not_alternatives":"(b) loses the symbolic intent; (c) means `count_generated` for *new* runs depends on whatever HEAD is at metrics time, which can differ from the actual fork point \u2014 see R-2.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":12,"event_id":"evt_20260524_212304_0012","run_id":"2026-05-24-fix-generated-lines-base-ref-head","at":"2026-05-24T21:23:04-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-002","decision":"Capture the SHA against the **source repo** at `/start` time, *before* the worktree exists. The lazy fallback in `lines.py` runs against the **worktree** at metrics time.","rationale":"At `/start`, the worktree doesn't exist yet \u2014 `git worktree add` is the call we're about to make. The source repo's `HEAD` is what `worktree add` will fork from, so it's the right boundary.","alternatives_considered":"Capture inside the worktree post-`worktree add`.","why_not_alternatives":"Same SHA either way for fresh forks, but the source-repo flow is the one we *want* to model. Lazy fallback uses the worktree because the source-repo path may no longer be reachable from `lines.py`'s perspective (and the existing code already operates inside the worktree).","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":13,"event_id":"evt_20260524_212304_0013","run_id":"2026-05-24-fix-generated-lines-base-ref-head","at":"2026-05-24T21:23:04-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-003","decision":"Make `base_ref_sha` an optional metadata field; gate the lazy resolver on \"field absent.\" Don't error out if it's absent \u2014 fall back transparently.","rationale":"Migration story for existing runs without an explicit one-shot script. Brief: \"Lazy resolver is simpler \u2014 recommended.\"","alternatives_considered":"One-shot migration script that touches every `runs/*/metadata.yaml`.","why_not_alternatives":"Brief explicitly chose lazy. Touching old metadata files violates \"no rewrites\" non-goal.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":14,"event_id":"evt_20260524_212304_0014","run_id":"2026-05-24-fix-generated-lines-base-ref-head","at":"2026-05-24T21:23:04-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-004","decision":"Both `count_generated` and `count_accepted` get the new `base_ref_sha` parameter, even though the brief only calls out `count_generated` explicitly.","rationale":"`count_accepted` has the same `<base_ref>...<sha>` bug for any run that landed a merge SHA but had `base_ref=\"HEAD\"`. Fix the pattern in both places now.","alternatives_considered":"Fix only `count_generated`.","why_not_alternatives":"Leaves the same hole in `accepted_lines`. Cost of fixing both is small.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":15,"event_id":"evt_20260524_212304_0015","run_id":"2026-05-24-fix-generated-lines-base-ref-head","at":"2026-05-24T21:23:04-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-005","decision":"The lazy fallback uses `git rev-parse` inside the **worktree**, not the source repo. If that fails or returns empty, fall back to the *symbolic* `base_ref` (today's behavior).","rationale":"`lines.py` already operates inside the worktree (the `-C worktree_path` flag is on every git call). Reaching into the source repo from `lines.py` requires extra plumbing for `metadata.target.repo.path` and adds a failure mode (source repo deleted, moved, etc.). Per R-2, the lazy resolver is best-effort by design.","alternatives_considered":"Lazy resolution against the source repo via `metadata.target.repo.path`.","why_not_alternatives":"More plumbing, more failure modes, the brief's wording is \"lazy resolver in `lines.py` that calls `git rev-parse` inside the worktree.\"","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
